# LLM work log (GitHub: turibiusrozario-tutorials)

## 2026-11-03 — confirmation links: multi-account fix, coalitions, one editor at a time, extra point people (branch claude/pensive-curie-slxv45)
- Request (5 items): links fail with 2+ Google accounts; coalitions need links; warn/take over when two people edit; two more point people; best way to reach off without a phone.
- Why the page moved: script.google.com web-app pages show "Sorry, unable to open the file at this time" when several Google accounts are signed in (a long-standing Google bug the script can't fix). The page is now `confirm.html` on the map site and calls the same web app with fetch and `credentials: "omit"`, so Google sign-in state doesn't matter (the map's live data already loads this way).
- Decisions (asked first): move to the map site; one editor + autosave + first submit wins (replaces per-card holds); a coalition's page shows every item tagged with it; keep the cap of 3 point people.
- Built by sub-agents against one written contract (back end: Confirm.gs/Code.gs/tests/SETUP.md; front end: confirm.html/src/confirm.ts/vite.config.ts), then reviewed: fixed a stale-page hole in first-submit-wins and autosave overwriting the Links notes.
- Links spreadsheet (private): link column now points to confirm.html?t=<token> (formula of the token until the menu "Update confirmation link addresses" is run), new "kind" column, 8 coalition rows added with new tokens. No tokens or emails in the repo.
- Not testable from here: the real Google CORS path for POST (the GET path is confirmed: 302 with Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *). Check one link after deploying.

## 2026-11-05 — sign-in on the map: Google + "Confirm with email" (branch claude/beautiful-cori-m2l55k)
- Request: "Sign in with Google" top right; when signed in and the email is on file, no "Continue to the Google Form" step; otherwise "Confirm with email" (15-minute magic link, 30-day sign-in), plus a setting for which account sends the emails.
- Decisions (asked first): all four + forms; "on file" = point person of the group picked in the form; not on file → Needs Review; the link submits the waiting form automatically; neutral wording (don't reveal whose email is on file); a "Log in" button on the link's page (scanners); Sign out; Google Form kept as backup; regular Gmail team account via "Send mail as" (Nathan is making it).
- Server: new `apps-script/SignIn.gs` (doPost actions google / emailLink / login / submitForm). Google ID tokens checked with Google's tokeninfo against `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID`; sessions are HMAC-signed tokens (`SESSION_SECRET`, made automatically) good for 30 days; login links are 128-bit tokens in CacheService for 15 minutes, one use. Submissions go through processSubmission_ unchanged; only real question titles get through (cleanForm_), so internal fields like `__coalition_id` can't be set from the site.
- Emails not on file get no email (no spam vector) and their form waits in Needs Review with no email in the payload, so a later Editors change can't auto-apply it for an address nobody confirmed. Caps: 3 links per address per 15 min, 20 unconfirmed forms an hour.
- `sendMail_` in Code.gs now sends every automated email: `MAIL_FROM` (must be a verified "Send mail as" address of the deployer, checked with GmailApp.getAliases, else reply-to), `MAIL_NAME`, `MAIL_REPLY_TO`. Note: using GmailApp adds a Gmail permission to the script.
- Did it myself rather than with a Sonnet sub-agent: the work was mostly security-sensitive glue across files I already had in context; a sub-agent would have had to re-read Code.gs (2.7k lines) and I'd have re-reviewed it anyway.
- Tests: new "sign-in OK" block in tests/apps-script.test.cjs (fake Utilities/UrlFetchApp/GmailApp). Site checked in Playwright with the web app mocked (forms, login page over the loading screen, phone width). Not testable here: real Google sign-in, real email delivery to Hotmail/Yahoo, tokeninfo from Apps Script.
